  "body": "(fork synced at v0.16.0)\n\nImplements a dedicated post-processor dialect for Doosan DNM vertical machining centers with Fanuc 0i / 31i-M controls (#614).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`**:\n  - Clean-room implementation specced from published Fanuc 0i-MODEL F operator programming manuals, Renishaw MP700 / Inspection Plus manuals, DN Solutions Operation Manual `MV0009OPE241_v0`, and real Doosan DNM machine sample program from Issue #614.\n  - **High-Speed Smoothing / AICC (`G5.1 Q1 Rx` / `G5.1 Q0`):** Modal Fanuc AI Contour Control lookahead smoothing with machining condition selection (levels `R1` to `R10`, default `R5` matching the real Doosan DNM sample program). Automatically deactivated (`G5.1 Q0`) prior to canned drilling cycles (`G73`, `G81-G89`), probing, tool change, and program close. Out-of-range smoothing levels are strictly refused by name.\n    * *Citation:* FANUC Series 0i-MODEL F Operator's Manual (B-64604EN-2/01) §3.3 (p. 19/33, p. 20/34), §3.3.2 (p. 22/36), §14.1 (p. 377–386). Requires Fanuc AICC I (A02B-0340-S603) or AICC II (A02B-0340-S605).\n  - **Renishaw Inspection Plus Probing (`G65 P9832` / `G65 P9833`):** Emits `G65 P9832` (probe optical turn-on) on its own block before protected positioning moves (`G65 P9810`) and surface measurement (`G65 P9811`), and emits `G65 P9833` (probe optical turn-off / sleep) on its own block at the end of the probing sequence before spindle stop/retract. Unknown probing styles are strictly refused by name.\n    * *Citation:* Renishaw MP700 Probe System Installation and User's Guide (H-2000-5142-02-A) Chapter 4 (p. 4-2 to 4-17) and Chapter 5.\n  - **Rotary Table Brake (4th-axis A on separate blocks, no name sniffing):** Emits `M11` (unclamp) on its own separate block before rotary positioning, and `M10` (clamp) on its own separate block after positioning before cutting (never inline with motion blocks). Continuous 4th-axis contouring unclamps before motion and restores clamping at section end. Strict refusal by name if undeclared via options/properties (`rotaryClamp`/`rotaryUnclamp` or `rotaryBrake`) or machine definition.\n    * *Citation:* DN Solutions Operation Manual `MV0009OPE241_v0` Part 5 §3 (p. 180) and Part 8 §3 (p. 232) Alarm 2323.\n  - **Chip Conveyor Codes & Strict Refusal:** Requires codes to be declared via post options (`chipConveyorStart` / `chipConveyorStop`), properties, or machine definition, and strictly refuses undeclared codes by name.\n    * *Citation:* DN Solutions Operation Manual `MV0009OPE241_v0` Part 5 §3 (p. 180) and Part 5 §2.13 (p. 137).\n  - **Through-Spindle Coolant (TSC) & Strict Refusal:** Emits Doosan high-pressure TSC M-code `M88` (with `M89`/`M09` on shut-off) when declared in the machine coolants table, or `M8` when `useM8ForTSC` is enabled. Strictly refuses undeclared through-tool coolant by name if the machine lacks a through-tool entry.\n    * *Citation:* DN Solutions Operation Manual `MV0009OPE241_v0` Part 5 §3 (p. 180) and Part 6 §2.6 (p. 217).\n  - **Manifest cleanup:** Removed unverified `axisInversion` and `probeAxisInversion` manifest flags pending mirrored-stream equivalence test goldens.\n- **`docs/evidence/614-dnm5700-sample.nc`**:\n  - In-tree real-world sample G-code program provided by community user `@spikeypineapple` on Issue #614 comment 6764944619 confirming real-world DNM 5700 syntax for `G5.1 Q1 R5`, `M07`, and Renishaw Inspection Plus macros.\n- **`assets/machines/doosan-dnm.mch`**:\n  - Registered in `posting::MACHINES` and `crates/app/tests/machine.rs` as `\"Doosan DNM 5700\"` (Kind: Mill).\n  - Updated with official DN Solutions DNM 4500/5700/6700 Specification Catalog numbers (X/Y/Z: 1020/570/510 mm, rapids: 36/36/30 m/min, cutting feed: 15 m/min, spindle: 40-12000 RPM, 18.5 kW, rigid tapping, 30-tool ATC, coolants M8/M7/M88, 4th-axis rotary table A).\n- **Decision Record**:\n  - Recorded in `docs/decisions/614-doosan-dnm-post.md` with all manual citations, page numbers, and design choices.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **`crates/app/tests/doosan_dnm_post.rs`** (7/7 passing):\n  - `doosan_dnm_posts_basic_milling_clean`: basic program structure, preamble, tool change, work offset, retracts, safe end.\n  - `doosan_dnm_through_spindle_coolant_modes`: verifies M88/M89 default TSC and M8 option.\n  - `doosan_dnm_rotary_brake_clamp_unclamp`: verifies separate block emission (`M11`, motion block, `M10`) around A-axis moves with `rotaryBrake: true`.\n  - `doosan_dnm_high_speed_smoothing_aicc`: verifies `G5.1 Q1 R5` engagement, `G5.1 Q0` deactivation before canned drilling cycles, and custom level `G5.1 Q1 R8`.\n  - `doosan_dnm_chip_conveyor`: verifies M31 start and M33 stop with explicit configuration.\n  - `doosan_dnm_probing_modes`: verifies `G65 P9832` (probe on) before moves and `G65 P9833` (probe off) at end.\n  - `doosan_dnm_refuses_undeclared_codes_by_name`: verifies strict refusal by name for undeclared TSC, undeclared rotary clamp (tested on both generic VMC and DNM machine to ensure no name sniffing), unknown probing style, unbounded smoothing level, and undeclared chip conveyor codes.\n- **`crates/app/tests/machine_library.rs`** (11/11 passing):\n  - `every_machine_file_in_assets_is_in_the_library`: verifies Doosan DNM 5700 machine is mounted and registered.\n- **`crates/app/tests/machine.rs`** (33/33 passing):\n  - `every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration`: pinned Doosan DNM 5700.\n- **`crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`** (6/6 passing):\n  - `every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact` across all goldens.\n  - `every_builtin_registry_entry_compiles`, `every_builtin_declares_its_controls_file_extension`, `the_dialects_actually_differ`.\n- Clippy `-D warnings` is completely clean.\n\nChangelog: Doosan DNM post processor aligned with real machine sample program and manual citations (G5.1 Q1 R<n> smoothing, Inspection Plus G65 P9832/P9833 probe on/off, separate block M10/M11 rotary clamp, and strict refusal of undeclared codes) (#614)\n\nFixes #614\n",
